<h3>Introduction</h3>
<p>The Include Shared Block Macro is simliar to the
Confluence Excerpt Include - but instead of pulling in 
the contents of the first discovered Excerpt Macro it pulls
in the contents of either the first discovered Shared Block 
Macro or the specified Shared Block Macro.  This ability to
target a particular Shared Block rather than the first one
is what gives this macro purpose.</p>
<h3>Usage</h3>
<p>In the macro parameters, the page on which the shared
block is defined needs to be specified.  Optinally, the
key identifying the shared block may be provided.  The key
is a string that needs to match in both the Shared Block
and the Include Shared Block before the contents may be
pulled in. If no key is specified, the contents of the
first Shared Block on the page will be pulled in.</p>
